NOTE FOR PARTICIPANTS — READ BEFORE COPYING THE JSON BELOW
===========================================================
This file is the complete, correct configuration for Windows.
It contains two comment blocks (lines beginning with NOTE:) to explain
what each section does. JSON does not support comments natively — these
lines are here for your understanding only.

⚠️  IMPORTANT: If you copy this entire file into Notepad, you MUST delete
    all comment lines (any line starting with NOTE:) before saving.
    A valid mcp.json must contain JSON only — no plain-text notes.
    The clean JSON-only version starts after the dashed line below.

Substitutions required (two changes only):
  1. Replace  tvly-YOUR_TAVILY_API_KEY_HERE  with your actual Tavily key
     (it starts with tvly- and was copied from app.tavily.com)
  2. Replace  C:\\Users\\YOUR_USERNAME\\Documents\\ARK-Industries\\
     with the actual path to the folder containing your ARK Industries files

⚠️  BACKSLASH RULE: Every \ in a Windows path must be written as \\ in JSON.
    File Explorer shows:   C:\Users\Joan\Documents\ARK-Industries
    In this file you type: C:\\Users\\Joan\\Documents\\ARK-Industries
    Using single backslashes will cause an ENOENT error and the Filesystem
    MCP will not connect.

-----------------------------------------------------------------------

{
  "mcpServers": {

    "tavily": {
      "command": "npx",
      "args": ["-y", "tavily-mcp@0.1.4"],
      "env": {
        "TAVILY_API_KEY": "tvly-YOUR_TAVILY_API_KEY_HERE"
      }
    },

    "filesystem": {
      "command": "npx",
      "args": [
        "-y",
        "@modelcontextprotocol/server-filesystem",
        "C:\\Users\\YOUR_USERNAME\\Documents\\ARK-Industries\\"
      ]
    }

  }
}

-----------------------------------------------------------------------

LINE-BY-LINE EXPLANATION (for reference — not part of the JSON)
================================================================

"mcpServers"
  The top-level key that LM Studio reads to find your MCP tool
  configurations. Everything sits inside this block.

"tavily"
  The name LM Studio uses to identify this tool. You will see
  "mcp/tavily" appear in the Integrations panel when it connects.

"command": "npx"
  Tells LM Studio to use Node.js's npx runner to launch this server.
  You do not need to understand npx — Node.js (installed in Phase 1)
  handles this automatically.

"args": ["-y", "tavily-mcp@0.1.4"]
  Downloads and runs version 0.1.4 of the Tavily MCP server package.
  The -y flag means "yes, install automatically without asking".

"TAVILY_API_KEY": "tvly-YOUR_TAVILY_API_KEY_HERE"
  Replace the placeholder with your actual key from app.tavily.com.
  The key must stay inside the double quotes.

"filesystem"
  The name LM Studio uses to identify the file access tool. You will
  see "mcp/filesystem" in the Integrations panel when it connects.

"@modelcontextprotocol/server-filesystem"
  The official open-source Filesystem MCP server package, maintained
  by Anthropic. This is what gives the AI read access to your folder.

"C:\\Users\\YOUR_USERNAME\\Documents\\ARK-Industries\\"
  Replace this with the path to your ARK Industries folder —
  using double backslashes throughout.
  Example (if your Windows username is jsmith):
    "C:\\Users\\jsmith\\Documents\\ARK-Industries\\"
  If your Documents folder is on OneDrive:
    "C:\\Users\\jsmith\\OneDrive\\Documents\\ARK-Industries\\"
  Copy the path directly from the File Explorer address bar,
  then manually double every backslash.
